From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David <dfattal@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 09:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(android): the display_transform log says "0 = NONE" but
 NONE is 1

gfx::OverlayTransform starts at OVERLAY_TRANSFORM_INVALID = 0, so
OVERLAY_TRANSFORM_NONE is 1 and ROTATE_CLOCKWISE_90 is 4. The log line added
in 0091 tells the reader "0 = NONE; anything else means the buffer is
PRE-ROTATED", which is wrong in the most damaging possible direction: it
labels the ONE healthy value (1) as a fault, and it reads a genuine
90-degree pre-rotation (4) as just another non-zero number.

This is not hypothetical. A tester's capture showed both values on the same
device — `1600x2414 display_transform=1` and `1454x2560 display_transform=4`
— and the message led the first reader (me) to conclude the device was
pre-rotated in both, when in fact one was the correct, untransformed case
and the difference between them was the whole finding.

State the enum name instead of inviting arithmetic on a value whose base the
message gets wrong.
---
 .../display_embedder/skia_output_surface_impl_on_gpu.cc | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/components/viz/service/display_embedder/skia_output_surface_impl_on_gpu.cc b/components/viz/service/display_embedder/skia_output_surface_impl_on_gpu.cc
--- a/components/viz/service/display_embedder/skia_output_surface_impl_on_gpu.cc
+++ b/components/viz/service/display_embedder/skia_output_surface_impl_on_gpu.cc
@@ -489,8 +489,13 @@ void SkiaOutputSurfaceImplOnGpu::Reshape(
     LOG(WARNING) << "[DisplayXR] android weave: root render pass "
                  << size_.ToString() << " display_transform="
                  << static_cast<int>(params.transform)
-                 << " (0 = NONE; anything else means the buffer is PRE-ROTATED "
-                    "and its orientation does not match the physical panel)";
+                 << " ("
+                 << (params.transform == gfx::OVERLAY_TRANSFORM_NONE
+                         ? "NONE: buffer matches the physical panel"
+                         : "PRE-ROTATED: buffer orientation does NOT match the "
+                           "physical panel. gfx::OverlayTransform starts at "
+                           "INVALID=0, so NONE=1 and ROTATE_CLOCKWISE_90=4")
+                 << ")";
   }
 #endif
   if (!output_device_->Reshape(params)) {
